<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via 7-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via 7-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system on Thursday through seven-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at 5-7/16 percent, below the Fed's 5-1/2 percent target for the rate, at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1679 ))</p>
</text>
